# Day 33 — what never enters the build context.
#
# A build context is a tar of everything not listed here, sent to the daemon
# before the first `RUN`. On this tree that is 40 MB of history, test fixtures,
# rendered docs and caches for a wheel that needs eleven directories, and it is
# also the surface a stray secret can leak through. `tools/docker_packaging.py`
# fails the build when one of the required patterns below disappears.
#
# The builder stage copies its paths explicitly, so nothing here can remove a
# file the image needs — and the audit cross-checks exactly that, because a
# `COPY` of an ignored path silently produces an empty layer rather than an
# error.

# --- version control and GitHub metadata -----------------------------------
.git
.github
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# --- environments and caches ----------------------------------------------
.venv
venv
env
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mutmut_cache/
mutants/
build/
dist/
site/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
benchmark-results*.json
*.log

# --- developer-only trees --------------------------------------------------
tests/
docs/
benchmarks/
tools/
docker/

# --- secrets and local configuration --------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
secrets*

# --- container plumbing ----------------------------------------------------
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
